## Exemple de integrare

Valorile sunt demonstrative. Înlocuiește ID-urile și folosește doar propriile permisiuni.

### cURL

```sh
curl --fail-with-body -X POST https://openaliment.ro/api/v2/manage/label-validations \
  -H 'Accept: application/json' \
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN' \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  --data '{"version_key":"E1","name":"Iaurt natural","category":"lactate","ingredients":"Lapte, culturi lactice.","allergens":"Lapte.","net_quantity":"200 g","operator":"Denumirea și adresa operatorului"}'
```

### JavaScript

```javascript
const response = await fetch("https://openaliment.ro/api/v2/manage/label-validations", {
  method: "POST",
  credentials: "omit",
  headers: {
  "Accept": "application/json",
  "Authorization": "Bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN",
  "Content-Type": "application/json"
},
  body: JSON.stringify({
  "version_key": "E1",
  "name": "Iaurt natural",
  "category": "lactate",
  "ingredients": "Lapte, culturi lactice.",
  "allergens": "Lapte.",
  "net_quantity": "200 g",
  "operator": "Denumirea și adresa operatorului"
})
});
const result = await response.json();
if (!response.ok) throw new Error(result.message || result.error_description || ('HTTP ' + response.status));
console.log(result);
```

### Python

```python
import json, urllib.request, urllib.parse, urllib.error

headers = {'Accept': 'application/json', 'Authorization': 'Bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN', 'Content-Type': 'application/json'}
payload = json.loads('{"version_key": "E1", "name": "Iaurt natural", "category": "lactate", "ingredients": "Lapte, culturi lactice.", "allergens": "Lapte.", "net_quantity": "200 g", "operator": "Denumirea și adresa operatorului"}')
data = json.dumps(payload).encode("utf-8")
request = urllib.request.Request('https://openaliment.ro/api/v2/manage/label-validations', data=data, headers=headers, method='POST')
try:
    with urllib.request.urlopen(request, timeout=15) as response:
        print(json.load(response))
except urllib.error.HTTPError as error:
    print(error.code, error.read().decode("utf-8", errors="replace"))
    raise
```

